# Git Flow + Commitizen

Always follow **Git Flow** for branches and **Commitizen / Conventional Commits** for messages.

The line that matters is **what reaches `origin`**, the fork [vs-76/quickfast-ng](https://github.com/vs-76/quickfast-ng): `develop` and `master` there change **only via PR**. Locally, integrating side branches into `develop` is allowed — see *Local integration* below.

- Author commits only on side branches (`feature/`, `bugfix/`, `hotfix/`, `release/`). Never write a commit while on `develop`/`master`/`main`; if asked to, stop, warn, and switch to a side branch.
- Never push `develop`, `master` or `main`, and never push a side branch straight into them.
- Local merge commits on `develop` are the one exception to "no commits on `develop`".
- "Merge into" targets in the table below name the PR that lands the branch, not a direct push.

## Branching (Git Flow)

| Purpose | Branch from | Branch name | Merge into |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| New feature | `develop` | `feature/<short-name>` | `develop` |
| Non-urgent bugfix | `develop` | `bugfix/<short-name>` | `develop` |
| Production hotfix | `master` | `hotfix/<short-name>` | `master` **and** `develop` |
| Release prep | `develop` | `release/<x.y.z>` | `master` **and** `develop` |

- Default working base is `develop`.
- Tag releases on `master` after a release/hotfix merge (`vX.Y.Z`).
- Do not invent ad-hoc branch names (`fix`, `wip`, bare ticket IDs alone).

```bash
# ✅ feature work
git checkout develop && git pull
git checkout -b feature/decoder-timeout
# ... commit on feature/decoder-timeout ...
git push -u origin feature/decoder-timeout   # then open PR to develop (or master for hotfix)

# ❌ wrong
git checkout -b my-fix
git commit            # on develop/master directly
git push origin develop
```

## Local integration (no push)

When asked to bring work "to local `develop`", "without pushing", or to integrate a
stack of branches, merge locally and stop there. This is expected, not a violation.

```bash
# ✅ local integration
git checkout develop
git merge --no-ff bugfix/dst-rotation-schedule
cmake --build build-dev-final -j && ctest --test-dir build-dev-final   # verify the merge
# stop here — no push
```

- Use `--no-ff` so every integration stays one reviewable unit.
- Verify the **merged** result, not just the branch that was merged.
- Keep the side branch: its PR is what actually lands the change upstream.
- `develop` sitting ahead of `origin/develop` is a normal outcome; do not "fix" it by pushing.
- Say plainly that the merge is local only, so it is not mistaken for a landed change.

## Pull requests (fork)

- Base repo is always [vs-76/quickfast-ng](https://github.com/vs-76/quickfast-ng) — never the OCI upstream (see `no-upstream-oci-writes`).
- Push the **side branch**, never `develop`, then open the PR against `develop` (or `master` for a hotfix).
- One PR per side branch. If local `develop` already holds several local merges, open a PR per branch instead of pushing `develop`.
- A hotfix needs two PRs: into `master` and into `develop`.

```bash
# ✅ landing a branch
git push -u origin bugfix/dst-rotation-schedule
gh pr create --repo vs-76/quickfast-ng --base develop --head bugfix/dst-rotation-schedule

# ❌ never
git push origin develop            # bypasses review
gh pr create --repo objectcomputing/quickfast ...
```

## Commits (Commitizen)

Use Conventional Commits. Prefer `git cz` / `cz commit` when available; otherwise write the same format by hand.

```
<type>(<optional-scope>): <imperative summary>

[optional body]

[optional footer]
```

**Types:** `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `chore`, `revert`

**Rules:**
- Summary ≤ ~72 chars, imperative (“add”, not “added”), no trailing period
- Scope optional but preferred when clear (`codec`, `decoder`, `docs`)
- Breaking change: `!` after type/scope **or** `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer
- One logical change per commit; do not mix unrelated edits

```
# ✅
feat(decoder): add template version guard
fix(codec): handle empty presence map
docs: clarify Git Flow merge targets

# ❌
Updated stuff
WIP
fixed bug
```

When the user asks to commit, draft a Commitizen-style message and follow the repo’s existing commit-message user rules (HEREDOC, no amend unless allowed, etc.).
